1
00:01:21,448 --> 00:01:24,179
Dad, I got your cleaning.

2
00:01:24,351 --> 00:01:25,410
Dad!

3
00:01:25,586 --> 00:01:28,066
All right! Don't move! Stay
right there and you won't get hurt.

4
00:01:28,221 --> 00:01:29,581
- Okay. Okay.
- Put that down.

5
00:01:29,723 --> 00:01:31,282
Turn around, hands
behind your back.

6
00:01:31,458 --> 00:01:33,458
- Get the tape out!
- What is it? What do you want?

7
00:01:33,627 --> 00:01:36,324
It's a kidnapping! Now, come
on. Let's go! Move! Move!

8
00:01:36,496 --> 00:01:38,988
Hiya, Ben. TRACEY: Aah!

9
00:01:45,539 --> 00:01:48,907
Aah! Barry, stop it!
Stop shooting, Barry!

10
00:01:49,076 --> 00:01:51,276
- Where is she? Where'd she go?
- She went out the back!

11
00:01:51,411 --> 00:01:52,879
Well, why didn't you stop her?

12
00:01:53,046 --> 00:01:56,380
You wouldn't stop shooting, I was
scared you were gonna shoot me!

13
00:01:56,550 --> 00:01:58,246
Well, go get her!

14
00:01:58,418 --> 00:02:01,411
Well, what am I supposed to do, just
tackle her in somebody's backyard?

15
00:02:01,588 --> 00:02:03,580
And drag her back to the van?

16
00:02:04,958 --> 00:02:08,793
- Face it, she's gone! We blew it.
- Wait! Get up!

17
00:02:08,962 --> 00:02:13,263
- Get up!
- Aah! Oh, my God, he's got a gun!

18
00:02:13,433 --> 00:02:18,235
- Put it down! Put it down!
Put it down! TRACEY: Aah!

19
00:02:20,107 --> 00:02:21,803
That's a drill, not a gun.

20
00:02:23,777 --> 00:02:26,474
- What's your name, anyway?
- Billy Lewis, friend of Ben's.

21
00:02:26,647 --> 00:02:27,842
What are you doing here?

22
00:02:28,015 --> 00:02:31,281
- Returning the drill.
- Returning a drill?

23
00:02:31,451 --> 00:02:33,215
- You borrow his tools often?
- All the time.

24
00:02:33,387 --> 00:02:35,627
- You must be a good friend of his.
- Since grade school.

25
00:02:35,756 --> 00:02:37,622
Tape please.

26
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:02,005
I don't know about this, Barry.

27
00:03:02,182 --> 00:03:03,844
- Sit down. Right here.
- The idea

28
00:03:04,017 --> 00:03:06,213
was to kidnap Matlock's
daughter, not some old geezer.

29
00:03:06,386 --> 00:03:07,513
What is the difference?

30
00:03:07,688 --> 00:03:09,288
What do you think he's
gonna do? Not pay?

31
00:03:09,456 --> 00:03:12,016
You think he's gonna say, "Go
ahead, blow my friend's brains out,

32
00:03:12,159 --> 00:03:14,519
I don't care." Now keep the
gun on him while I call Matlock.

33
00:03:14,661 --> 00:03:18,496
- And take that stupid hat off it.
- I don't have the gun. You do.

34
00:03:18,665 --> 00:03:21,225
- I gave it to you.
- No. You didn't, Barry.

35
00:03:21,401 --> 00:03:23,597
You put it on the floor,
so you could drive.

36
00:03:24,705 --> 00:03:26,298
Shut up.

37
00:03:34,181 --> 00:03:35,945
I will be right back.

38
00:03:51,264 --> 00:03:52,994
Leanne, are you here?

39
00:03:55,836 --> 00:03:58,101
- Thank God you're home.
- What happened?

40
00:03:58,271 --> 00:04:01,598
Cliff, I... Um...

41
00:04:04,478 --> 00:04:07,073
I um... I think Billy
was kidnapped.

42
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:09,648
- What? LEANNE: I
came over to the house

43
00:04:09,816 --> 00:04:12,536
to drop off your dry cleaning and
these two people burst in the door,

44
00:04:12,686 --> 00:04:14,120
and they started
waving a gun around

45
00:04:14,287 --> 00:04:15,880
and saying they were
going to kidnap me,

46
00:04:16,056 --> 00:04:21,893
and then Billy came in and
surprised them and all hell broke loose.

47
00:04:24,431 --> 00:04:28,630
I threw your dry cleaning
over the guy's head

48
00:04:28,802 --> 00:04:31,328
and then over the gun so
that Billy and I could get away.

49
00:04:31,505 --> 00:04:33,497
Wait, they shot at you?

50
00:04:34,441 --> 00:04:37,172
Well, the gun went
off a couple of times.

51
00:04:37,344 --> 00:04:39,245
I don't think he was
aiming at anything.

52
00:04:39,412 --> 00:04:44,214
Aw. You must have
been scared to death.

53
00:04:44,384 --> 00:04:45,909
What about my dad?

54
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:49,112
Okay. All right, let's see.

55
00:04:49,289 --> 00:04:50,757
Well, I went out the back door.

56
00:04:50,924 --> 00:04:53,450
I thought that Billy would
go out the front door.

57
00:04:53,627 --> 00:04:55,755
When I came back five
minutes later, they were gone,

58
00:04:55,929 --> 00:04:58,262
- and so was he.
- His car's still out front.

59
00:04:58,431 --> 00:05:01,230
I know. But what I'm saying, Dad,
is when they couldn't kidnap me,

60
00:05:01,401 --> 00:05:03,199
I guess they
kidnapped Billy instead.

61
00:05:03,370 --> 00:05:04,668
Did you call the police?

62
00:05:04,838 --> 00:05:07,205
No. I wanted to wait
and talk to you first.

63
00:05:07,374 --> 00:05:10,902
I can't believe someone just came
in here and kidnapped my own father.

64
00:05:17,617 --> 00:05:20,018
Hello? BARRY: <i>Ben Matlock?</i>

65
00:05:20,187 --> 00:05:22,884
- Yes.
- I'm here with an old friend of yours.

66
00:05:23,056 --> 00:05:25,218
Just a second. I'll put him on.

67
00:05:25,392 --> 00:05:28,385
All right, you say
hello and don't get cute.

68
00:05:28,562 --> 00:05:29,928
Ben?

69
00:05:30,096 --> 00:05:31,587
They're holding
a gun on me, Ben.

70
00:05:31,765 --> 00:05:33,927
Billy, what's going
on? Where are you?

71
00:05:35,302 --> 00:05:37,737
- You there?
- What do you want?

72
00:05:37,904 --> 00:05:40,339
Five hundred thousand dollars.

73
00:05:40,507 --> 00:05:42,032
Five hundred thousand dollars!

74
00:05:42,209 --> 00:05:45,441
<i>In old, unmarked,
non-sequential bills.</i>

75
00:05:46,479 --> 00:05:48,311
That's a half million dollars.

76
00:05:48,481 --> 00:05:53,943
You have exactly 24 hours to get it.
If you do not have it by then, he dies.

77
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:58,922
If you call the police, the
FBI, or anyone else, he dies.

78
00:05:59,092 --> 00:06:03,496
If you tamper with the
money in any way, he dies.

79
00:06:04,397 --> 00:06:06,423
You getting all
this, Mr. Matlock?

80
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:08,728
You want a half
million dollars for Billy?

81
00:06:08,902 --> 00:06:11,337
<i>In 24 hours. I'll be in touch.</i>

82
00:06:11,504 --> 00:06:13,439
Oh, and by the way,

83
00:06:13,607 --> 00:06:18,045
I would save the cheap tricks
for court if I were you, slimeball.

84
00:06:22,949 --> 00:06:25,475
- He's gone.
- Oh.

85
00:06:25,652 --> 00:06:29,714
This is awful. This is awful.
What are we gonna do?

86
00:06:29,890 --> 00:06:31,324
Okay, okay, okay.

87
00:06:31,491 --> 00:06:33,483
I really feel like we
should call the police.

88
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:35,219
No, no, you didn't
hear what he said?

89
00:06:35,395 --> 00:06:37,762
No, no, he said he'd be
watching, he said he'd know.

90
00:06:37,931 --> 00:06:41,197
Listen, I saw these two people.
They are not professionals.

91
00:06:41,368 --> 00:06:44,668
- They're probably bluffing.
- Okay. Maybe they're bluffing.

92
00:06:44,838 --> 00:06:46,758
What if you're wrong?
What if my father dies? No!

93
00:06:46,907 --> 00:06:50,400
The only thing you can do, Ben,
you gotta give them the $500,000.

94
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:58,597
- What are you doing?
- Calling the police.

95
00:06:58,752 --> 00:07:00,778
- Ben!
- It's my $500,000.

96
00:07:00,954 --> 00:07:02,616
- I'm calling the police.
- Oh!

97
00:07:02,789 --> 00:07:04,485
Oh.

98
00:07:04,658 --> 00:07:08,390
Okay. By the end of the day
tomorrow, we'll be on our way to Rio.

99
00:07:08,561 --> 00:07:09,756
You dummy.

100
00:07:09,930 --> 00:07:12,297
You can't say things
like that in front of him.

101
00:07:12,465 --> 00:07:16,061
You two are kind of green at
this sort of thing, aren't you?

102
00:07:16,236 --> 00:07:18,517
Yeah. Well, maybe I don't
care what I say in front of you,

103
00:07:18,672 --> 00:07:20,641
because I might just
kill you for the fun of it.

104
00:07:20,807 --> 00:07:24,335
Even if we do get the
money. So don't try anything.

105
00:07:27,047 --> 00:07:29,516
- Oh! Barry. BARRY:
He did that on purpose.

106
00:07:29,683 --> 00:07:32,847
- I didn't do anything.
- Don't touch it! It hurts!

107
00:07:33,019 --> 00:07:34,544
You're getting a goose egg.

108
00:07:34,721 --> 00:07:37,486
Old goat could have fractured
my skull. You better watch it, pal.

109
00:07:37,657 --> 00:07:39,922
- Yeah.
- Careful.

110
00:07:40,093 --> 00:07:41,994
- Is it big?
- Baby.

111
00:07:42,162 --> 00:07:44,290
Ow! You watch
it, too, that hurts.

112
00:07:44,464 --> 00:07:46,126
That is where I hit my head.

113
00:08:01,348 --> 00:08:04,750
FBI, please hold. You
can go on in, Mr. Spiers.

114
00:08:06,252 --> 00:08:07,379
FBI. May I help you?

115
00:08:08,321 --> 00:08:10,321
- Dennis, good morning.
- Good morning, Alan.

116
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:11,822
Have a seat.

117
00:08:14,661 --> 00:08:16,027
Morning, Dennis.

118
00:08:17,597 --> 00:08:18,860
Ed.

119
00:08:19,399 --> 00:08:21,800
A man named Billy Lewis was
kidnapped yesterday morning

120
00:08:21,968 --> 00:08:24,665
over at Willow Springs. Atlanta
P.D.'s already on the case.

121
00:08:26,106 --> 00:08:27,972
They called us not just
as a matter of course,

122
00:08:28,141 --> 00:08:32,602
but because the man who received
the ransom instructions is Ben Matlock.

123
00:08:32,779 --> 00:08:35,248
Defense attorney who
specializes in murder one cases.

124
00:08:35,415 --> 00:08:37,475
Lots of connections in
state and local government.

125
00:08:37,650 --> 00:08:38,913
Thank you, Ed.

126
00:08:39,085 --> 00:08:40,383
Media is still in the dark.

127
00:08:40,553 --> 00:08:42,749
But because this could
become a high-profile case,

128
00:08:42,922 --> 00:08:45,448
I want my best agents
handling it, and that's you two.

129
00:08:46,626 --> 00:08:48,618
Well, you're gonna have
to count me out, Alan.

130
00:08:48,795 --> 00:08:50,457
- I can't do it.
- Excuse me?

131
00:08:50,630 --> 00:08:53,225
Well, for one thing, I'm
still on the Sanborn case.

132
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,840
We'll have Simpson
take over for you.

133
00:08:55,001 --> 00:09:00,702
No. I can't work with Ed,
Alan. I'm sorry. I just... I can't.

134
00:09:00,874 --> 00:09:02,240
Not after what
happened last time.

135
00:09:03,610 --> 00:09:05,250
I thought you two had
worked through that.

136
00:09:06,046 --> 00:09:08,743
With all due respect, it's
real hard to work through

137
00:09:08,915 --> 00:09:13,046
- being made a laughing stock like that.
- It was an honest mistake.

138
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:16,314
You chased, tackled and cuffed
an undercover police officer

139
00:09:16,489 --> 00:09:18,048
in front of four TV cameras.

140
00:09:18,224 --> 00:09:20,216
He matched the
description of the perp.

141
00:09:20,393 --> 00:09:24,262
Yeah. Well, for weeks I
had to watch myself on TV

142
00:09:24,431 --> 00:09:26,662
helping you make complete
asses out of both of us.

143
00:09:26,833 --> 00:09:28,495
Take it easy, Dennis.

144
00:09:29,736 --> 00:09:31,227
Obviously, this
isn't going to work.

145
00:09:31,404 --> 00:09:35,364
I don't need a partner, Alan, I
can handle this case on my own.

146
00:09:35,542 --> 00:09:37,875
Well, you're going to have to.

147
00:09:38,044 --> 00:09:40,013
Agent Spiers, one minute.

148
00:09:41,147 --> 00:09:44,675
Here's the name and number
of your contact at A.P.D.

149
00:09:49,722 --> 00:09:51,520
I'm there.

150
00:10:02,936 --> 00:10:05,656
You and I will talk about this
later, Dennis, after you've cooled off

151
00:10:05,805 --> 00:10:09,242
and can be a little more
professional about it.

152
00:10:10,910 --> 00:10:12,469
Yes, sir.

153
00:10:18,017 --> 00:10:20,953
There was no need to
embarrass me like that in there.

154
00:10:21,921 --> 00:10:23,913
I was just telling
it like it is, Ed.

155
00:10:24,090 --> 00:10:26,050
You're an over-zealous
buffoon who has no business

156
00:10:26,192 --> 00:10:27,717
being in this business.

157
00:10:55,722 --> 00:10:58,556
Ben! Ha-ha-ha.

158
00:10:58,725 --> 00:11:01,422
Ed Wingate, FBI. Pretend
I'm an old friend, invite me in.

159
00:11:01,594 --> 00:11:03,790
- Unh?
- They may be watching.

160
00:11:04,297 --> 00:11:05,788
Oh, John! John!

161
00:11:05,965 --> 00:11:07,297
- Come on in.
- How are you?

162
00:11:07,467 --> 00:11:11,097
Good. Come on in. Ha-ha-ha.

163
00:11:11,271 --> 00:11:14,639
Well done, Mr. Matlock, a
little overplayed, but well done.

164
00:11:14,807 --> 00:11:18,437
- Come on in.
- Detective Schroeder, how goes it?

165
00:11:18,611 --> 00:11:20,944
Wingate. They assigned
you to this case?

166
00:11:21,114 --> 00:11:23,447
- Right you are.
- You know each other?

167
00:11:23,616 --> 00:11:25,482
Worked together last
year. Linwood abduction.

168
00:11:25,652 --> 00:11:28,952
We cracked the case wide
open, didn't we, detective?

169
00:11:29,122 --> 00:11:32,251
Yeah, yeah. Come on.
I'll show you the setup.

170
00:11:37,297 --> 00:11:39,323
Look who the FBI
sent over, boys.

171
00:11:39,499 --> 00:11:42,697
Come on. Come on. Let's nip
the territorial squabbling in the bud.

172
00:11:42,869 --> 00:11:44,929
I'm here to help you.
You're here to help me.

173
00:11:45,104 --> 00:11:48,438
We're all here to see Mr. Lewis
comes home safely, right?

174
00:11:48,608 --> 00:11:51,009
- Right.
- I'm Cliff Lewis. I'm his son.

175
00:11:51,177 --> 00:11:52,475
Thank you very much for coming.

176
00:11:52,645 --> 00:11:56,980
Just doing my job, something
I do, fortunately, very well.

177
00:11:57,150 --> 00:11:59,745
There's a tap and tracer
on this phone. It's over here.

178
00:11:59,919 --> 00:12:00,943
This guy is great.

179
00:12:03,189 --> 00:12:04,953
Show time, everybody.

180
00:12:05,124 --> 00:12:07,389
Mr. Matlock, if
it's the kidnappers,

181
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:09,825
you'll have to keep them
on the phone for four minutes.

182
00:12:09,996 --> 00:12:12,591
- Four minutes?
- Pick it up, please.

183
00:12:14,067 --> 00:12:17,060
- Four minutes is a long time.
- Dad, let's go. Pick it up.

184
00:12:17,237 --> 00:12:19,297
What am I gonna talk
about for four minutes?

185
00:12:22,442 --> 00:12:23,466
Hello.

186
00:12:23,643 --> 00:12:25,612
<i>Here's what you're
gonna do with the money.</i>

187
00:12:25,778 --> 00:12:27,178
<i>You listening?</i>

188
00:12:29,382 --> 00:12:31,544
- Yes.
- There is a phone booth

189
00:12:31,718 --> 00:12:35,450
at a truck stop on Route
20, just past Eatonville.

190
00:12:35,622 --> 00:12:38,615
Be in it at 4:15 with the money

191
00:12:38,791 --> 00:12:40,817
and no funny stuff,
because I'll be watching.

192
00:12:41,661 --> 00:12:44,221
East Mill. Is that
what you said?

193
00:12:44,397 --> 00:12:45,660
No. Eatonville.

194
00:12:45,832 --> 00:12:50,928
E-T... E-A-T...
Eatonville! You know it.

195
00:12:51,104 --> 00:12:53,801
4:15, on the dot
or Billy bites it.

196
00:12:53,973 --> 00:12:57,410
Wa... Wait a minute, wait a
minute. Let me speak to him.

197
00:12:57,577 --> 00:13:02,015
- Put him on the phone.
- Aah, all right. Hold on.

198
00:13:03,082 --> 00:13:06,052
- Say something nice.
- Hello, Ben.

199
00:13:06,219 --> 00:13:10,179
- Billy, you okay?
<i>- Yeah. I'm okay.</i>

200
00:13:10,356 --> 00:13:14,657
<i>If you see Cliff, tell him to water
the lawn. He always forgets.</i>

201
00:13:15,595 --> 00:13:17,086
See, there he
is, alive and well.

202
00:13:17,263 --> 00:13:20,427
If you want him to stay that way,
you'll be in the phone booth at 4:15.

203
00:13:21,701 --> 00:13:24,865
Wait a minute. Wait a minute.
There's, uh... There's a problem.

204
00:13:25,038 --> 00:13:26,768
- What?
<i>- Uh...</i>

205
00:13:29,342 --> 00:13:31,311
I don't have the money.

206
00:13:32,312 --> 00:13:33,336
<i>You what?</i>

207
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:36,947
I don't have the $500,000.

208
00:13:37,116 --> 00:13:40,280
What are you talking about?
You make a hundred grand a case.

209
00:13:40,453 --> 00:13:42,888
Well, I've made
some bad investments.

210
00:13:43,056 --> 00:13:44,854
I mean, I could've
tried to fool you

211
00:13:46,626 --> 00:13:48,322
and given you a sack
full of play money.

212
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:53,990
But I'm trying to be honest
about this. I need more time.

213
00:13:54,167 --> 00:13:56,602
- Did you call the cops?
- No.

214
00:13:56,769 --> 00:13:57,964
You told me not to.

215
00:14:00,406 --> 00:14:03,501
You got 24 hours, you
piece of crud. That's it!

216
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:08,704
You get it?

217
00:14:08,881 --> 00:14:10,816
Why'd you tell him you
didn't have the money?

218
00:14:10,983 --> 00:14:13,452
Well, I was stalling. I
didn't know what else to say.

219
00:14:13,619 --> 00:14:15,554
Well, you could have
gotten him killed. Oh!

220
00:14:15,722 --> 00:14:19,853
The thing he said
about watering the lawn.

221
00:14:20,026 --> 00:14:22,826
It could have been some kind of
code. What could he have meant by that?

222
00:14:22,995 --> 00:14:24,675
I'm supposed to tell
you to water the lawn.

223
00:14:24,831 --> 00:14:27,062
Oh. I forgot.

224
00:14:30,403 --> 00:14:33,043
He doesn't have the money? He's
loaded. He's got to have the money.

225
00:14:33,206 --> 00:14:35,926
- He said he couldn't get it.
- Call him back and let me talk to him.

226
00:14:36,075 --> 00:14:38,374
- Shut up and relax.
- You don't know how to handle him.

227
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:40,445
- I do.
- I said shut up!

228
00:14:40,613 --> 00:14:42,013
Where's the gun?

229
00:14:42,181 --> 00:14:43,945
- It's on the counter.
- Thank you.

230
00:14:44,117 --> 00:14:46,882
- Barry. Barry, come on.
- What?

231
00:14:47,053 --> 00:14:50,319
Come here. Now, you
just take it easy, okay?

232
00:14:50,490 --> 00:14:52,516
Hang in there.

233
00:14:52,692 --> 00:14:55,218
One more day
and it'll all be over.

234
00:14:59,465 --> 00:15:00,990
Okay.

235
00:15:02,702 --> 00:15:04,694
- Barry.
- Hmm?

236
00:15:04,871 --> 00:15:07,340
What if Matlock doesn't
come up with the money?

237
00:15:08,941 --> 00:15:11,843
I just want to hit that
scum bucket where it hurts.

238
00:15:12,011 --> 00:15:14,173
If I can't do it by
taking his money,

239
00:15:14,347 --> 00:15:17,511
then I'm just gonna have to do
something else, something worse.

240
00:15:19,018 --> 00:15:20,816
I meant what I said.

241
00:15:20,987 --> 00:15:24,048
If he doesn't pay,
we kill the old man.

242
00:15:44,844 --> 00:15:46,836
Hello, Dennis. DENNIS: Alan.

243
00:15:47,013 --> 00:15:49,448
- Got a minute?
- Yeah. It's just about all I have.

244
00:15:49,615 --> 00:15:51,311
Come on in.

245
00:15:57,390 --> 00:15:59,256
I'm going right back
out to Sanborn's.

246
00:15:59,425 --> 00:16:01,917
Just came home to grab a
shower, change of clothes.

247
00:16:02,094 --> 00:16:04,996
- How are they doing?
- Well, they're going nuts.

248
00:16:05,164 --> 00:16:07,690
They're starting to treat
us like we're the bad guys.

249
00:16:07,867 --> 00:16:10,268
Kidnapper's supposed to
call about the drop tomorrow.

250
00:16:11,871 --> 00:16:13,703
This about Wingate?

251
00:16:13,873 --> 00:16:17,310
Look, uh, I realize the
man is a little eccentric.

252
00:16:17,477 --> 00:16:18,638
Yeah.

253
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:20,643
He works tirelessly
and he gets results.

254
00:16:20,813 --> 00:16:24,250
Even after that tackling incident, he
stuck with the case until it was solved.

255
00:16:24,417 --> 00:16:27,512
In fact, I wouldn't mind
having ten more just like him.

256
00:16:27,687 --> 00:16:29,849
That's because you don't
have to work with him.

257
00:16:30,022 --> 00:16:31,320
Dennis.

258
00:16:34,760 --> 00:16:37,889
Personality quirks aside,
Wingate is one of my best men.

259
00:16:38,764 --> 00:16:40,665
From now on, whomever
I assign to work with him

260
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:44,861
is gonna have to accept that
assignment or he's gonna be out.

261
00:16:45,972 --> 00:16:47,372
Is that clear?

262
00:16:48,674 --> 00:16:50,006
Yeah.

263
00:16:51,277 --> 00:16:52,609
Oh.

264
00:16:52,778 --> 00:16:55,748
I almost forgot. They
issued new pass keys today.

265
00:16:55,915 --> 00:16:58,248
You won't be able to get in
the garage tomorrow without it.

266
00:16:59,418 --> 00:17:01,387
Okay. Thanks.

267
00:17:01,554 --> 00:17:04,080
Dennis, you're a good man.

268
00:17:04,257 --> 00:17:06,590
Don't make me do
something we'll both regret.

269
00:17:08,327 --> 00:17:10,262
Luck with the Sanborns.

270
00:17:27,013 --> 00:17:30,450
Hey! Wake up.
Breakfast is served.

271
00:17:30,616 --> 00:17:32,209
Here we go.

272
00:17:33,219 --> 00:17:35,984
Aah. And around.

273
00:17:39,425 --> 00:17:40,757
Let's see here.

274
00:17:43,262 --> 00:17:46,255
Got you one of those croissant
and scrambled egg jobs.

275
00:17:48,401 --> 00:17:50,370
- Yuck.
- What yuck?

276
00:17:50,536 --> 00:17:53,136
I eat these all the time. They're
very good. Now, come on, eat it.

277
00:17:53,272 --> 00:17:56,401
- It's got cheese in it.
- What's wrong with cheese?

278
00:17:56,576 --> 00:17:58,704
- Gives me gas.
- Come on, eat it.

279
00:18:00,379 --> 00:18:02,974
Within about a half hour,
you're gonna be sorry.

280
00:18:03,950 --> 00:18:05,612
- Ow!
- What? What happened?

281
00:18:05,785 --> 00:18:07,651
- He bit me! He bit me.
- Oh.

282
00:18:07,820 --> 00:18:09,448
- What do you want me to do?
- Something!

283
00:18:09,622 --> 00:18:12,353
Look, he bit me clear down
to the bone. I'm bleeding.

284
00:18:12,525 --> 00:18:14,016
That's it.

285
00:18:17,196 --> 00:18:19,461
Starve to death for
all I care, you lunatic.

286
00:18:19,632 --> 00:18:21,863
- Here, give me this.
- I'm sorry, honey.

287
00:18:22,034 --> 00:18:25,232
Come over here, I'll wash it off.
- He hurt me.

288
00:18:30,009 --> 00:18:32,729
<i>They gotta know you're here.
That's why they haven't called.</i>

289
00:18:32,878 --> 00:18:35,404
- Come on, Dr. Sanborn. Take it easy.
- No!

290
00:18:35,581 --> 00:18:36,913
Get out of here! All of you!

291
00:18:37,083 --> 00:18:38,643
Just get out of here
and leave us alone.

292
00:18:38,818 --> 00:18:40,912
Look, they'll call.
I promise you.

293
00:18:41,087 --> 00:18:44,888
I can't take any more
of this. I just can't.

294
00:18:45,057 --> 00:18:46,081
Mrs. Sanborn.

295
00:18:56,068 --> 00:18:57,263
Ready.

296
00:19:02,208 --> 00:19:04,473
Hello. MATTHEW: <i>Dad.</i>

297
00:19:04,644 --> 00:19:07,170
Matthew! Are you okay, son?

298
00:19:07,346 --> 00:19:10,077
<i>Yeah. I'm supposed to
read something to you.</i>

299
00:19:11,250 --> 00:19:16,951
<i>"In exactly one hour, Mrs. Sanborn
is to leave the money on the ground</i>

300
00:19:17,123 --> 00:19:23,723
<i>directly behind the car parked in slot
142 in the Peel Lot in 19th and Grant.</i>

301
00:19:23,896 --> 00:19:27,389
<i>Make sure she comes alone.
Matthew won't be released</i>

302
00:19:27,566 --> 00:19:30,502
<i>until after I've examined
and counted the money.</i>

303
00:19:30,670 --> 00:19:34,107
<i>So don't try anything,
or you'll be very sorry."</i>

304
00:19:36,242 --> 00:19:37,335
Matthew?

305
00:19:40,413 --> 00:19:43,212
It's too short for a trace.

306
00:19:43,382 --> 00:19:45,142
But I'm gonna take
this tape down to the lab,

307
00:19:45,284 --> 00:19:47,244
see if they can ID any of
those background noises.

308
00:19:47,386 --> 00:19:49,048
- I'll handle the stake-out.
- No.

309
00:19:49,221 --> 00:19:51,053
No stake-out. You heard him.

310
00:19:51,223 --> 00:19:53,249
They want me to go there
alone. They might see you.

311
00:19:53,426 --> 00:19:57,056
They won't, Mrs. Sanborn.
You won't even see us.

312
00:20:26,258 --> 00:20:28,727
Mrs. Sanborn just made the drop.

313
00:20:28,894 --> 00:20:29,953
All units stand by.

314
00:20:30,129 --> 00:20:32,169
<i>Unit two standing by.</i>
AGENT 2: <i>Standing by.</i>

315
00:20:32,298 --> 00:20:33,857
<i>Unit one, roger.</i>

316
00:20:34,033 --> 00:20:35,899
Here comes a blue hatchback.

317
00:20:36,068 --> 00:20:38,003
<i>Unit one, I've got
the blue hatchback.</i>

318
00:20:39,605 --> 00:20:42,803
<i>- No pick-up. Still standing by.</i>
- No go.

319
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:58,186
Grey two-door Chevy approaching.

320
00:20:58,357 --> 00:21:00,087
<i>Unit one, I've got it.</i>

321
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:03,729
<i>Contact. We have
an affirmative pick-up.</i>

322
00:21:05,397 --> 00:21:07,332
It's him. Money's gone.

323
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:11,335
Okay, guys, we got him. Grey
two-door Chevy. License plate number...

324
00:21:12,171 --> 00:21:14,868
Great, he's got mud all over it.
Unit one, he's coming your way.

325
00:21:15,040 --> 00:21:16,872
<i>Unit one, roger.</i>

326
00:21:21,814 --> 00:21:24,875
No. Cancel that. He's doubling
back and heading toward the entrance.

327
00:21:25,050 --> 00:21:26,518
He's heading south down Grant.

328
00:21:27,987 --> 00:21:29,922
<i>Unit three in pursuit.</i>

329
00:21:34,293 --> 00:21:35,933
- Three, you got him?
<i>- We got him,</i>

330
00:21:36,095 --> 00:21:37,654
<i>a block ahead of us.</i>

331
00:22:56,575 --> 00:22:59,443
<i>This is unit three. We're on
Lincoln just north of Second.</i>

332
00:23:01,013 --> 00:23:02,379
<i>We lost him.</i>

333
00:23:05,651 --> 00:23:07,651
Check your levels.
- We're all set.

334
00:23:14,660 --> 00:23:16,288
Hello.

335
00:23:16,462 --> 00:23:18,055
<i>You got the money, Matlock?</i>

336
00:23:18,631 --> 00:23:24,133
Uh... Well... You
don't have the money?

337
00:23:24,303 --> 00:23:25,999
<i>Let me ask you something.</i>

338
00:23:26,171 --> 00:23:29,232
When's the last time
you tried to get your hands

339
00:23:29,408 --> 00:23:33,368
on a half million dollars
in non-sequential bills?

340
00:23:33,545 --> 00:23:36,413
- It's not that easy.
- Well, you had two days.

341
00:23:36,582 --> 00:23:38,676
- Let me talk to him.
- Shut up.

342
00:23:38,851 --> 00:23:42,310
Uh... You want me to kill this man,
Mr. Matlock? Is that what you want?

343
00:23:42,488 --> 00:23:45,481
- Because I will. Gladly.
- No, no!

344
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:51,628
No, no, no.

345
00:23:52,598 --> 00:23:57,262
It's just that...
Uh... Ahem. Uh...

346
00:23:57,436 --> 00:24:03,433
A half million dollars
is a lot of money.

347
00:24:04,510 --> 00:24:06,035
<i>Now...</i>

348
00:24:06,211 --> 00:24:12,048
if you had asked
for, say, $200,000,

349
00:24:13,419 --> 00:24:18,790
that would have taken some
time. But maybe I could swing that.

350
00:24:20,659 --> 00:24:22,753
You're negotiating?

351
00:24:22,928 --> 00:24:25,022
- Three hundred thousand?
- Two-fifty.

352
00:24:28,133 --> 00:24:30,329
All right, 250,000.
But by noon tomorrow.

353
00:24:30,502 --> 00:24:32,403
And if you do not have
it by then, so help me,

354
00:24:32,571 --> 00:24:35,006
I will put this old man on the
phone, and blow his brains out

355
00:24:35,174 --> 00:24:37,734
with you listening. You
got that, Mr. Sleaze?

356
00:24:43,315 --> 00:24:45,307
- No dice.
- I can't believe you did that.

357
00:24:45,484 --> 00:24:47,077
- Did what?
- Quibbled over money.

358
00:24:47,252 --> 00:24:48,550
- I wasn't quibbling.
- Quibbler!

359
00:24:48,721 --> 00:24:51,054
I wasn't quibbling.
I was stalling.

360
00:24:51,223 --> 00:24:54,250
Trying to keep him on the
line for Marcel Marceau here.

361
00:24:55,194 --> 00:24:57,527
Mr. Sleaze.

362
00:24:57,696 --> 00:25:04,159
And then he called you a slimeball
and referred to you as a piece of crud.

363
00:25:05,838 --> 00:25:09,605
It's personal with this guy. Now,
are you sure you don't recognize him?

364
00:25:09,775 --> 00:25:11,903
- Positive. Leanne?
- No.

365
00:25:12,678 --> 00:25:16,410
Somewhere, somehow, you
have had dealings with this man.

366
00:25:17,883 --> 00:25:20,216
Mark my words.

367
00:25:48,080 --> 00:25:51,312
- Matthew!
- Mommy! Mommy!

368
00:25:51,750 --> 00:25:53,309
- Oh, baby. Oh, baby.
- Aah!

369
00:25:53,485 --> 00:25:57,013
How you doing, son?
Gosh, it's good to see you.

370
00:25:57,322 --> 00:25:59,484
Oh, gosh.

371
00:26:00,592 --> 00:26:03,391
The kidnapper dropped
him off in a residential area,

372
00:26:03,562 --> 00:26:06,191
and Matthew had the smarts
to go to somebody's house

373
00:26:06,365 --> 00:26:09,085
- and ask him to call 911 for him.
- Thank you for bringing him home.

374
00:26:09,234 --> 00:26:10,634
Thank you for everything.

375
00:26:10,803 --> 00:26:13,898
We need to ask Matthew questions
while things are still fresh in his mind.

376
00:26:14,073 --> 00:26:16,599
So we can do that here,
or we can do it downtown.

377
00:26:16,775 --> 00:26:18,437
- Which would you prefer?
- Here.

378
00:26:18,610 --> 00:26:21,512
Because the instant you're
finished, we're going to Disneyland.

379
00:26:32,858 --> 00:26:36,590
There seem to be three sounds
or sound patterns to this thing.

380
00:26:36,762 --> 00:26:38,196
There's the kid.

381
00:26:38,363 --> 00:26:40,559
<i>In exactly one hour...</i>

382
00:26:40,732 --> 00:26:44,760
Then there's this one which
I've tweaked it just a tad.

383
00:26:46,271 --> 00:26:48,137
<i>- In exactly one hour...</i>
- What is that?

384
00:26:48,307 --> 00:26:50,538
Sounds like church bells.

385
00:26:51,176 --> 00:26:54,146
And finally there's this one,
also computer-enhanced.

386
00:26:54,313 --> 00:26:58,648
Bink, I need this analyzed ASAP.

387
00:26:58,817 --> 00:27:00,513
How's it going, Dennis?

388
00:27:00,686 --> 00:27:03,126
- Come on, come on, let's go.
- Actually, I've been working...

389
00:27:03,288 --> 00:27:05,018
If you'd take those
stupid sunglasses off,

390
00:27:05,190 --> 00:27:07,455
you might be able to see
that he's busy, Wingate.

391
00:27:09,761 --> 00:27:14,426
Matthew Sanborn has been
released. Billy Lewis has not.

392
00:27:14,600 --> 00:27:17,764
I believe that gives
my case priority.

393
00:27:18,637 --> 00:27:23,405
- Tough.
- That response is unacceptable.

394
00:27:25,477 --> 00:27:27,878
- Unh.
- You are unacceptable, Wingate,

395
00:27:28,046 --> 00:27:29,810
and I've had just
about all I'm gonna take.

396
00:27:35,254 --> 00:27:38,520
Bink, you want to throw
that on, see what we've got?

397
00:27:45,297 --> 00:27:46,492
All right. Come on, you guys.

398
00:27:46,665 --> 00:27:49,726
This stuff costs the
taxpayers a lot of money.

399
00:28:03,849 --> 00:28:06,785
Don't think this
is over, Spiers.

400
00:28:07,519 --> 00:28:09,545
Just get outta here.

401
00:28:22,467 --> 00:28:25,904
I don't know what it is about
that guy. He just makes me nuts.

402
00:28:27,739 --> 00:28:30,732
Well, assuming
I still have a job,

403
00:28:30,909 --> 00:28:32,275
where were we?

404
00:28:32,444 --> 00:28:33,969
You okay?

405
00:28:34,146 --> 00:28:35,341
- Yeah.
- Okay.

406
00:28:35,514 --> 00:28:37,745
All right, let's see where
we are in this thing.

407
00:28:39,751 --> 00:28:41,344
- We got the kid.
- Yeah.

408
00:28:41,520 --> 00:28:44,547
You got the church
bells. And we have this.

409
00:28:47,926 --> 00:28:50,327
That's construction.
Sounds like construction.

410
00:28:51,663 --> 00:28:54,223
Did that kid see anything?

411
00:28:54,399 --> 00:28:56,039
He saw the kidnapper
when he was snatched.

412
00:28:56,201 --> 00:28:58,136
The rest of the time
he was blindfolded.

413
00:29:00,305 --> 00:29:03,571
Thanks, Bink. I got
some phone calls to make.

414
00:29:03,742 --> 00:29:05,335
I'll see you later.

415
00:31:36,094 --> 00:31:38,757
No. He and his folks are
on their way to Disneyland.

416
00:31:38,930 --> 00:31:39,954
Yeah.

417
00:31:40,132 --> 00:31:43,762
I'm keeping it till the L.A. office can
pick them up and the kid can ID it.

418
00:31:43,935 --> 00:31:45,460
If this cap turns
out to be Matthew's,

419
00:31:45,637 --> 00:31:47,877
then that's gotta be the house
the kidnapper held him in.

420
00:32:00,619 --> 00:32:01,643
Right.

421
00:32:03,789 --> 00:32:06,122
Right. Yeah. I left the
sample in your box.

422
00:32:06,291 --> 00:32:08,123
Just analyze it first
thing in the morning.

423
00:32:08,293 --> 00:32:10,493
Hang on to the results. We
can find out who lives there.

424
00:32:12,297 --> 00:32:14,562
Great. Thanks, Bink.

425
00:32:15,767 --> 00:32:18,965
Okay. I'll see you
tomorrow. Night.

426
00:32:58,143 --> 00:33:00,223
His pockets been emptied.
His drawers rifled through,

427
00:33:00,378 --> 00:33:02,378
and according to the
neighbor that heard the shots,

428
00:33:02,547 --> 00:33:04,573
there used to be a
television right there.

429
00:33:05,817 --> 00:33:07,683
Looks like he walked
in on a burglar.

430
00:33:09,054 --> 00:33:10,647
Six years with the bureau.

431
00:33:11,723 --> 00:33:13,248
Out in the field every day.

432
00:33:14,259 --> 00:33:17,855
Coming up against everything
from gunrunners to paid assassins.

433
00:33:18,797 --> 00:33:20,857
How does he die?
In his own home.

434
00:33:21,533 --> 00:33:24,196
Fighting off some punk
looking for drug money.

435
00:33:25,437 --> 00:33:27,030
What a world.

436
00:33:48,393 --> 00:33:50,225
That stuff stinks.

437
00:33:50,962 --> 00:33:54,524
I got news for you. So do you.

438
00:33:57,035 --> 00:33:59,163
Well, well, well,
look who's awake.

439
00:33:59,971 --> 00:34:01,940
- Want a donut?
- Yes, please.

440
00:34:02,107 --> 00:34:03,541
I don't think so.

441
00:34:04,476 --> 00:34:06,809
Today's the day. Here you go.

442
00:34:06,978 --> 00:34:11,439
If Matlock shafts me this time,
you're a dead man, and that's a fact.

443
00:34:12,183 --> 00:34:13,378
Jackass.

444
00:34:14,452 --> 00:34:16,182
Did you just call me a jackass?

445
00:34:16,354 --> 00:34:19,586
No. I called that jackass
Ben Matlock a jackass.

446
00:34:19,758 --> 00:34:21,488
Jackass Matlock?

447
00:34:21,660 --> 00:34:23,026
I thought he was
your best friend.

448
00:34:23,194 --> 00:34:24,685
He's not my best friend.

449
00:34:24,863 --> 00:34:28,197
Just because I known him for a
long time doesn't mean I like him.

450
00:34:28,366 --> 00:34:34,237
In fact, after all this, I like that
cheap little backstabber less than ever.

451
00:34:34,406 --> 00:34:36,500
Well you couldn't like
him any less than I like him.

452
00:34:36,675 --> 00:34:40,771
Yeah? That bum left my
sister, Lucy, at the altar.

453
00:34:40,946 --> 00:34:43,006
She was so heartbroken,
she moved in with me.

454
00:34:43,982 --> 00:34:46,542
Didn't move out for 40
years. Ruined my whole life.

455
00:34:47,218 --> 00:34:49,551
Yeah? Well, he sent my
brother to prison for 25 years.

456
00:34:49,721 --> 00:34:51,656
- Barry!
- I'm not gonna tell him his name.

457
00:34:51,823 --> 00:34:54,793
That's not as bad as
40 years with Lucy.

458
00:34:58,096 --> 00:35:01,794
I wish I could see his face when
he turns over that 250 grand.

459
00:35:01,967 --> 00:35:03,936
It would kill
him. Just kill him.

460
00:35:04,102 --> 00:35:05,161
You think so?

461
00:35:05,337 --> 00:35:08,830
Why, turning over $2.50
would kill that tightwad.

462
00:35:09,007 --> 00:35:11,567
Really, you think?

463
00:35:13,044 --> 00:35:17,243
Why, I could tell you stories
about greed and parsimony

464
00:35:17,415 --> 00:35:21,250
that would curl your toes.
- Yeah?

465
00:35:22,187 --> 00:35:23,712
Tell us some.

466
00:35:24,489 --> 00:35:27,789
Where to begin, where to begin?

467
00:35:29,227 --> 00:35:33,187
- Agent Spiers is dead?
- Yes.

468
00:35:33,365 --> 00:35:34,628
He left me a message last night

469
00:35:34,799 --> 00:35:38,702
saying he had gotten a lead in the
Sanborn case and was gonna call you.

470
00:35:38,870 --> 00:35:40,930
- Did he?
- Yeah.

471
00:35:41,106 --> 00:35:44,304
He said he found a baseball
cap in some house somewhere.

472
00:35:44,476 --> 00:35:46,968
Thought it might belong
to the Sanborn kid.

473
00:35:47,145 --> 00:35:50,138
Also found a puddle of oil that
he thought might have come

474
00:35:50,315 --> 00:35:53,114
from the kidnapper's car. Told me
he was gonna leave a sample of it

475
00:35:53,284 --> 00:35:55,844
here in the lab so I could
analyze it first thing in the morning.

476
00:35:55,987 --> 00:35:59,014
- That's what I'm doing.
- He found Matthew's baseball cap?

477
00:35:59,190 --> 00:36:02,957
He didn't know it was his. But he
was gonna keep it till the kid could ID it.

478
00:36:03,128 --> 00:36:05,393
My men didn't find any
baseball cap at Spiers' place.

479
00:36:05,563 --> 00:36:08,089
What time was it when
he called? You remember?

480
00:36:08,533 --> 00:36:11,594
Well, I just turned the TV off.
So it must have been around 10.

481
00:36:11,770 --> 00:36:14,239
The same time the neighbor
said he heard the shots.

482
00:36:14,406 --> 00:36:16,726
Did he indicate anything was
wrong or hear anything unusual

483
00:36:16,875 --> 00:36:18,355
- while you were talking to him?
- No.

484
00:36:18,510 --> 00:36:20,536
He had Beethoven
blaring in the background.

485
00:36:20,712 --> 00:36:22,840
- Same as always.
- Beethoven?

486
00:36:23,014 --> 00:36:26,416
- Yeah, the fourth, I think.
- That's kind of funny.

487
00:36:26,584 --> 00:36:29,884
Burglars don't usually enter a house
when they know somebody's there.

488
00:36:30,055 --> 00:36:32,286
You think someone intended
to confront Dennis Spiers?

489
00:36:32,457 --> 00:36:34,824
I don't know. It's possible the
guy who wound up killing him

490
00:36:34,993 --> 00:36:37,861
made it look like a burglary
and he covered his trail.

491
00:36:38,029 --> 00:36:40,157
You guys know anybody who
may have had it out for him?

492
00:36:40,331 --> 00:36:43,130
No. He was a great guy,
got along with everybody.

493
00:36:43,301 --> 00:36:45,293
No. That's not quite true.

494
00:36:47,672 --> 00:36:51,439
He had a fight with another agent
in this very room just yesterday.

495
00:36:51,609 --> 00:36:52,872
Who was the other agent?

496
00:36:54,112 --> 00:36:55,546
Ed Wingate.

497
00:36:58,216 --> 00:37:03,348
All right, everybody. It is
imperative that we stay focused.

498
00:37:03,521 --> 00:37:05,820
I know it's difficult,
but we must.

499
00:37:07,258 --> 00:37:09,989
Don't you ever take
off those dark glasses?

500
00:37:10,161 --> 00:37:12,756
Is there a glare in my house?

501
00:37:14,165 --> 00:37:16,259
It's 12:21. Something's wrong.

502
00:37:16,434 --> 00:37:18,665
- Relax, Cliff.
- They said they would call at noon.

503
00:37:18,837 --> 00:37:19,896
They're kidnappers.

504
00:37:20,071 --> 00:37:23,735
Keeping their word is
probably not a big deal to them.

505
00:37:23,908 --> 00:37:26,400
Are you sure that all
the money's in here?

506
00:37:26,578 --> 00:37:28,012
It's there.

507
00:37:29,080 --> 00:37:31,777
12:22. Why haven't they called?

508
00:37:41,626 --> 00:37:43,857
I can't believe it.
He shot the moon.

509
00:37:44,028 --> 00:37:46,497
I haven't shot the moon
since I was 14 years old.

510
00:37:46,664 --> 00:37:48,826
- I have never shot the moon.
- That is amazing.

511
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:50,195
How many points is that?

512
00:37:50,368 --> 00:37:54,703
That's, uh, minus 26 for each
of you and a big fat zero for me.

513
00:37:54,873 --> 00:37:56,774
- Unbelievable.
- Okay.

514
00:37:56,941 --> 00:37:58,671
Who wants a Swiss
cheese sandwich?

515
00:37:58,843 --> 00:38:01,711
Tracy, Billy can't have
cheese, remember?

516
00:38:01,880 --> 00:38:04,315
Oh. Yeah, I'm sorry.

517
00:38:04,482 --> 00:38:07,042
Um, would peanut
butter and jelly be okay?

518
00:38:07,218 --> 00:38:10,814
- Tuna fish would be better.
- Coming right up.

519
00:38:10,989 --> 00:38:13,788
- We got time for another hand?
- I think so.

520
00:38:13,958 --> 00:38:17,986
Oh, my gosh. It's 12:30.

521
00:38:19,364 --> 00:38:20,764
- We got a call.
- This is it.

522
00:38:26,237 --> 00:38:29,537
- Um, hello.
- You got the money?

523
00:38:29,707 --> 00:38:31,676
Yeah. I got it.

524
00:38:31,843 --> 00:38:34,244
<i>Two hundred and fifty
thousand dollars, cash.</i>

525
00:38:34,412 --> 00:38:35,436
Yeah.

526
00:38:40,385 --> 00:38:42,786
All right, then, listen up.
This is what you're gonna do.

527
00:39:05,243 --> 00:39:08,111
- Hello. BARRY:
<i>Take off your clothes.</i>

528
00:39:08,279 --> 00:39:09,303
What?

529
00:39:09,480 --> 00:39:11,120
I gotta see whether
you're wearing a wire.

530
00:39:11,249 --> 00:39:12,877
<i>I'm not wearing a wire!</i>

531
00:39:13,051 --> 00:39:15,384
Yeah? Well, then
prove it. And hurry up.

532
00:39:27,298 --> 00:39:28,322
He's doing it.

533
00:39:35,006 --> 00:39:37,134
I'm only doing this once.

534
00:39:46,684 --> 00:39:48,653
He's clean.

535
00:39:52,757 --> 00:39:54,020
Now what?

536
00:39:54,192 --> 00:39:57,390
Very good, dirt bag.
Now, you leave the money.

537
00:39:57,562 --> 00:40:00,623
You tuck your shirt back in. You
get in the car and you drive home.

538
00:40:00,798 --> 00:40:04,394
- What about Billy?
- We see the money, you'll see him.

539
00:40:29,794 --> 00:40:31,990
We did it! He's gone! - Aah!

540
00:40:49,113 --> 00:40:51,605
Hurry up, go get the money.
- Okay.

541
00:41:07,865 --> 00:41:08,958
Is that him?

542
00:41:14,906 --> 00:41:16,636
Sure is.

543
00:41:45,570 --> 00:41:46,594
Aah! BARRY: Shh.

544
00:41:46,771 --> 00:41:48,933
Shh.

545
00:41:51,142 --> 00:41:52,940
Oh.

546
00:41:53,111 --> 00:41:54,477
Look at that.

547
00:41:54,645 --> 00:41:56,477
Oh. You did it.

548
00:41:56,647 --> 00:41:58,287
Couldn't have done it
without you, my man.

549
00:41:58,449 --> 00:42:00,213
- Oh, my pleasure.
- Whoo!

550
00:42:00,385 --> 00:42:04,652
I guess I'd better say adios
and let you kids get going.

551
00:42:06,491 --> 00:42:09,393
I'm sorry about biting
your finger like that.

552
00:42:09,560 --> 00:42:12,155
That's all right. I probably
would've done the same thing.

553
00:42:12,330 --> 00:42:14,026
See you around, Billy.

554
00:42:14,198 --> 00:42:16,326
Goodbye, Billy.

555
00:42:22,173 --> 00:42:23,539
Thanks.

556
00:42:27,879 --> 00:42:29,472
FBI.

557
00:42:29,647 --> 00:42:32,207
Put your hands on your
head, and keep them there.

558
00:42:33,284 --> 00:42:34,616
Now!

559
00:43:19,430 --> 00:43:22,264
May I help you, or
are you just browsing?

560
00:44:11,916 --> 00:44:13,942
He didn't even speak.

561
00:44:15,119 --> 00:44:17,350
He didn't thank me.
He didn't say anything.

562
00:44:17,522 --> 00:44:19,320
He acted like I wasn't there.

563
00:44:19,490 --> 00:44:22,255
Being kidnapped is a
very traumatic experience.

564
00:44:22,426 --> 00:44:25,658
- I'm sure he was under terrible stress.
- Well, we all were.

565
00:44:26,364 --> 00:44:28,595
Hello again, Mr. Matlock,
Miss Mclntyre.

566
00:44:28,766 --> 00:44:32,100
Your back door was
open, relatively speaking.

567
00:44:32,803 --> 00:44:34,829
Well, who's been kidnapped now?

568
00:44:35,006 --> 00:44:38,135
Actually, I'm here
on a personal matter.

569
00:44:38,309 --> 00:44:40,505
I believe I'm being
framed for murder.

570
00:44:41,412 --> 00:44:43,506
- Oh.
- Ah...

571
00:44:44,415 --> 00:44:47,317
I'm fairly certain that ballistics
will show that this weapon

572
00:44:47,485 --> 00:44:50,455
was used to kill an FBI agent
by the name of Dennis Spiers.

573
00:44:50,621 --> 00:44:52,419
He was shot to death
in his home last night.

574
00:44:52,590 --> 00:44:56,755
- My goodness.
- Anyway, about three hours ago,

575
00:44:56,928 --> 00:45:02,595
I found someone planting that
in the kitchen drawer at my home.

576
00:45:02,767 --> 00:45:06,204
I gave chase, but was
unable to apprehend him.

577
00:45:06,370 --> 00:45:10,569
Then I discovered that the police
had left a message on my machine

578
00:45:10,741 --> 00:45:14,269
saying they wanted to
question me about Dennis.

579
00:45:15,346 --> 00:45:20,580
Now, were I to deliver that to the
police, I would be arrested on the spot.

580
00:45:20,751 --> 00:45:24,415
Were I to not deliver it, I
would be obstructing justice,

581
00:45:24,589 --> 00:45:26,683
a thing equally objectionable.

582
00:45:26,857 --> 00:45:29,884
Ergo, I'd like it if
you would deliver it.

583
00:45:30,061 --> 00:45:34,556
Ergo, shmergo, the police
just want to question you.

584
00:45:34,732 --> 00:45:36,360
They don't want
to string you up.

585
00:45:36,534 --> 00:45:38,969
They probably want to question
everybody in your department.

586
00:45:39,136 --> 00:45:43,198
Take off those stupid sunglasses.
It's darker than pitch outside.

587
00:45:46,577 --> 00:45:47,636
Oh.

588
00:45:47,812 --> 00:45:49,838
Dennis Spiers did this to me.

589
00:45:50,014 --> 00:45:52,813
We got in an argument
at headquarters.

590
00:45:54,318 --> 00:45:58,653
I believe that whoever really
killed Dennis found about it

591
00:45:58,823 --> 00:46:02,487
and concluded that framing
me would take the heat off him.

592
00:46:04,428 --> 00:46:07,626
I am going to find that person.

593
00:46:09,200 --> 00:46:13,331
In the meantime, I believe
the police officer called,

594
00:46:13,504 --> 00:46:16,064
said his name was
Lieutenant Bronson.

595
00:46:16,240 --> 00:46:18,539
You can't do this. If you
don't talk to the police,

596
00:46:18,709 --> 00:46:20,229
you're gonna look
all the more guilty.

597
00:46:20,378 --> 00:46:23,405
I'm being realistic,
Miss Mclntyre.

598
00:46:23,581 --> 00:46:30,215
You see, the police don't like
me, nor do most of my co-workers.

599
00:46:30,388 --> 00:46:34,052
Were I to be
arrested and charged,

600
00:46:34,225 --> 00:46:39,129
I would be, to use the
vernacular, shafted.

601
00:46:39,297 --> 00:46:41,789
But the police are
gonna be looking for you.

602
00:46:41,966 --> 00:46:43,730
They're bound to catch you.

603
00:46:43,901 --> 00:46:44,994
No, they won't.

604
00:46:45,603 --> 00:46:51,270
You see, I am the wind.

605
00:46:54,245 --> 00:46:58,842
You know, you really ought
to do something about that.

606
00:46:59,750 --> 00:47:01,275
What?

607
00:47:04,722 --> 00:47:06,816
Well, I never.

608
00:47:06,991 --> 00:47:08,755
He's the wind.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
